  {"comment": "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT"},
  {"comment": "The bottle of a forum post (mitcad#2373, follow-up of mitcad#2320), built from scratch: four sections and two mirrored spline rails. Sketch1 F1 on XY: a 100 x 50 rectangle round the origin, its corners rounded by 10 (points p1 to p12; lines c13, c15, c17, c19 counter-clockwise from the bottom one, arcs c14, c16, c18, c20 after each: points and curves share one numbering). Plane1 F2 100 mm up and Sketch2 F3 on it: the same at 150 x 75. Plane2 F4 200 mm up and Sketch3 F5 on it: a circle of diameter 30; Plane3 F6 230 mm up and Sketch4 F7 on it: the same. Sketch5 F8 on XZ, upright (its y along +Z, the frame a sketch made in the application has): the rail c13, a spline through (50, 0), (75, 100), (30, 130), (15, 170), (15, 200), (15, 230), through the middles of the rectangles' short sides and points of the circles, and c14, its mirror image. Loft1 F9 through the four sections along both rails with Tangent Edges Merge, Loft2 F10 the same with Keep. Both failed with 'the loft could not be bent to follow its rails'. tools/cli/loft-rails-reported-test.py runs this script and checks each body against its mirror image and the rails on it; `mitcad-cli run` of this script with --save makes the design kept with the reported cases."},
